Matrix calculator - solves matrix operations with any method you like.

The following operations are available in this matrix calculator:
- Solving systems of linear equations using:
    * Gaussian elimination;
    * Cramer's rule;
    * Gauss-Jordan;
    * The inverse matrix method;
    * Montante (Bareiss algorithm);
- Finding the determinant of a matrix using:
    * Decomposition;
    * Reduction to triangular form;
    * Montante (Bareiss algorithm);
    * Sarrus' rule (only for a 3x3 matrix);
- Finding the inverse of a matrix using:
    * Gaussian elimination;
    * Gauss-Jordan;
    * Algebraic complements;
    * Montante (Bareiss algorithm);
- Finding the rank of a matrix using:
    * Elementary transformations;
    * Bordering minors;
- QR decomposition:
    * Gram–Schmidt;
    * Householder reflections;
    * Givens rotation;
- Polar decomposition;
- The square root of the matrix;
- Singular value decomposition;
- Eigenvalues;
- Eigenvectors;
- Eigendecomposition(matrix diagonalization);
- Matrix minor;
- Matrix cofactor;
- Matrix adjoint;
- LU decomposition;
- Schur Decomposition;
- Cholesky decomposition;
- Solving matrix equations;
- Raising a matrix to a power;
- Multiplying a matrix by a number;
- Matrix transposition;
- Matrix multiplication;
- Matrix subtraction;
- Matrix addition;

App Features
- Custom keyboard for more convenient data entry;
- Complete, step by step description of solutions;
- Ability to save solutions;
- Ability to edit saved solutions;
- Works without internet access;
- Presents solutions as ordinary and decimal fractions;
